---@class cloudflare.radar.AiTimeseriesGroupsTimeseriesRequest
---@field aggInterval? cloudflare.radar.AiTimeseriesGroupsTimeseriesRequestAggInterval|string Aggregation interval of the results (e.g., in 15 minutes or 1 hour intervals). Refer to [Aggregation intervals](https://developers.cloudflare.com/radar/concepts/aggregation-intervals/). When omitted, the interval is auto-selected from the requested date range; finer intervals are only available for shorter ranges. If the requested interval is too granular for the date range, the request is rejected.
---@field asn? cloudflare.radar.AiTimeseriesGroupsTimeseriesRequestAsnList Filters results by Autonomous System. Specify one or more Autonomous System Numbers (ASNs) as a comma-separated list. Prefix with `-` to exclude ASNs from results. For example, `-174, 3356` excludes results from AS174, but includes results from AS3356.
---@field contentType? cloudflare.radar.AiTimeseriesGroupsTimeseriesRequestContentTypeList Filters results by content type category. When set, results can only be further filtered by location, continent, or Autonomous System.
---@field continent? cloudflare.radar.AiTimeseriesGroupsTimeseriesRequestContinentList Filters results by continent. Specify a comma-separated list of alpha-2 codes. Prefix with `-` to exclude continents from results. For example, `-EU,NA` excludes results from EU, but includes results from NA.
---@field crawlPurpose? cloudflare.radar.AiTimeseriesGroupsTimeseriesRequestCrawlPurposeList Filters results by bot crawl purpose.
---@field dateEnd? cloudflare.radar.AiTimeseriesGroupsTimeseriesRequestDateEndList End of the date range (inclusive). Alternative to `dateRange`; provide together with `dateStart`. When requesting comparison series, every series must resolve to the same duration as the main series. Each `dateStart`/`dateEnd` is floored to the nearest 15 minutes before evaluation, so windows whose durations match only before alignment may be rejected.
---@field dateRange? cloudflare.radar.AiTimeseriesGroupsTimeseriesRequestDateRangeList Filters results by relative date range ending at the current time, with each value producing a separate series. Use `<n>d` for days (up to `364d`) or `<n>w` for weeks (up to `52w`). Append `control` to request the equivalent previous period for comparison: the comparison window is shifted back by the current window's length rounded up to a whole number of weeks, so it keeps the same weekday alignment and does not overlap the current window (e.g. `7dcontrol` covers days -14 to -7, `10dcontrol` covers days -24 to -14). For example, pass `7d` and `7dcontrol` to compare this week with the previous week. All series must resolve to the same duration as the main series; relative ranges (including `control`) satisfy this automatically. Use this parameter or set specific start and end dates (`dateStart` and `dateEnd` parameters).
---@field dateStart? cloudflare.radar.AiTimeseriesGroupsTimeseriesRequestDateStartList Start of the date range. Alternative to `dateRange`; provide together with `dateEnd`. When requesting comparison series, every series must resolve to the same duration as the main series. Each `dateStart`/`dateEnd` is floored to the nearest 15 minutes before evaluation, so windows whose durations match only before alignment may be rejected.
---@field format? cloudflare.radar.AiTimeseriesGroupsTimeseriesRequestFormat|string Format in which results will be returned.
---@field industry? cloudflare.radar.AiTimeseriesGroupsTimeseriesRequestIndustryList Filters results by industry.
---@field limitPerGroup? number Limits the number of objects per group to the top items within the specified time range. When item count exceeds the limit, extra items appear grouped under an "other" category. Only supported on high-cardinality dimensions; otherwise the request is rejected. Minimum value is 2.
---@field location? cloudflare.radar.AiTimeseriesGroupsTimeseriesRequestLocationList Filters results by location. Specify a comma-separated list of alpha-2 codes. Prefix with `-` to exclude locations from results. For example, `-US,PT` excludes results from the US, but includes results from PT.
---@field name? cloudflare.radar.AiTimeseriesGroupsTimeseriesRequestNameList Array of names used to label the series in the response.
---@field responseStatus? cloudflare.radar.AiTimeseriesGroupsTimeseriesRequestResponseStatusList Filters results by HTTP response status code (e.g. 200, 403, 404). Only [IANA-registered codes](https://www.iana.org/assignments/http-status-codes/http-status-codes.xhtml) are accepted.
---@field responseStatusCategory? cloudflare.radar.AiTimeseriesGroupsTimeseriesRequestResponseStatusCategoryList Filters results by HTTP response status code category.
---@field userAgent? cloudflare.radar.AiTimeseriesGroupsTimeseriesRequestUserAgentList Filters results by user agent.
---@field vertical? cloudflare.radar.AiTimeseriesGroupsTimeseriesRequestVerticalList Filters results by vertical.

