---@class cloudflare.radar.PostQuantumTlsSupportResponseBugs
---@field hrrFailure boolean Server sends a HelloRetryRequest but fails to complete the handshake after the client sends the second ClientHello. Often caused by non-compliant TLS 1.3 implementations on shared hosting providers.
---@field splitClientHello boolean Server rejects fragmented ClientHello caused by large PQ keyshare, but accepts classical (non-PQ) handshakes. Typically caused by middleboxes or firewalls that cannot reassemble split TLS ClientHello messages.
---@field unknownKeyshare boolean Server cannot handle an unknown key exchange algorithm in the ClientHello keyshare extension. Compliant servers should respond with HelloRetryRequest for a supported algorithm.

