---@field asn? cloudflare.radar.DnsTimeseriesGroupsProtocolRequestAsnList Filters results by Autonomous System. Specify one or more Autonomous System Numbers (ASNs) as a comma-separated list. Prefix with `-` to exclude ASNs from results. For example, `-174, 3356` excludes results from AS174, but includes results from AS3356.
---@field continent? cloudflare.radar.DnsTimeseriesGroupsProtocolRequestContinentList Filters results by continent. Specify a comma-separated list of alpha-2 codes. Prefix with `-` to exclude continents from results. For example, `-EU,NA` excludes results from EU, but includes results from NA.
---@field dateEnd? cloudflare.radar.DnsTimeseriesGroupsProtocolRequestDateEndList End of the date range (inclusive). Alternative to `dateRange`; provide together with `dateStart`. When requesting comparison series, every series must resolve to the same duration as the main series. Each `dateStart`/`dateEnd` is floored to the nearest 15 minutes before evaluation, so windows whose durations match only before alignment may be rejected.
---@field dateRange? cloudflare.radar.DnsTimeseriesGroupsProtocolRequestDateRangeList Filters results by relative date range ending at the current time, with each value producing a separate series. Use `<n>d` for days (up to `364d`) or `<n>w` for weeks (up to `52w`). Append `control` to request the equivalent previous period for comparison: the comparison window is shifted back by the current window's length rounded up to a whole number of weeks, so it keeps the same weekday alignment and does not overlap the current window (e.g. `7dcontrol` covers days -14 to -7, `10dcontrol` covers days -24 to -14). For example, pass `7d` and `7dcontrol` to compare this week with the previous week. All series must resolve to the same duration as the main series; relative ranges (including `control`) satisfy this automatically. Use this parameter or set specific start and end dates (`dateStart` and `dateEnd` parameters).
---@field dateStart? cloudflare.radar.DnsTimeseriesGroupsProtocolRequestDateStartList Start of the date range. Alternative to `dateRange`; provide together with `dateEnd`. When requesting comparison series, every series must resolve to the same duration as the main series. Each `dateStart`/`dateEnd` is floored to the nearest 15 minutes before evaluation, so windows whose durations match only before alignment may be rejected.
---@field format? cloudflare.radar.DnsTimeseriesGroupsProtocolRequestFormat|string Format in which results will be returned.
---@field location? cloudflare.radar.DnsTimeseriesGroupsProtocolRequestLocationList Filters results by location. Specify a comma-separated list of alpha-2 codes. Prefix with `-` to exclude locations from results. For example, `-US,PT` excludes results from the US, but includes results from PT.
---@field name? cloudflare.radar.DnsTimeseriesGroupsProtocolRequestNameList Array of names used to label the series in the response.
---@field nodata? cloudflare.radar.DnsTimeseriesGroupsProtocolRequestNodataList Specifies whether the response includes empty DNS responses (NODATA).
---@field queryType? cloudflare.radar.DnsTimeseriesGroupsProtocolRequestQueryTypeList Filters results by DNS query type.
---@field responseCode? cloudflare.radar.DnsTimeseriesGroupsProtocolRequestResponseCodeList Filters results by DNS response code.
---@field tld? cloudflare.radar.DnsTimeseriesGroupsProtocolRequestTldList Filters results by top-level domain. Incompatible with the `ipVersion`, `protocol`, `dnssecE2e`, `dnssecAware`, `responseTtl`, and `cacheHit` filters/dimensions; this restriction does not apply to country-code TLDs (2-letter, e.g. `uk`).

